// expect: error assert:assertion.false @ L50
// S48 (g) twin: m[0][3] on int m[2][3]: the first bound passes, the second (against the row's length, `... whose second index may be outside m[0]`) fails alone.
// (hand-written spike fixture of record 0064 (draft), not emitted by the tool and not checked by lint_viper.py; no `define`: every row is expanded as lowering will write it; no inhale or assume)
field v_int: Int
field d_int: Bool
field lv: Bool

// cerastes:domain-ok 0028
domain Block {
  function loc(b: Block, i: Int): Ref
  function len(b: Block): Int
  function block_of(r: Ref): Block
  function offset_of(r: Ref): Int
  function member(r: Ref, k: Int): Block
  function parent_of(b: Block): Ref
  function index_of(b: Block): Int
  function lvloc(b: Block): Ref
  // cerastes:axiom-ok 0033
  axiom loc_inv { forall b: Block, i: Int :: { loc(b, i) } block_of(loc(b, i)) == b && offset_of(loc(b, i)) == i }
  // cerastes:axiom-ok 0034
  axiom loc_nonnull { forall b: Block, i: Int :: { loc(b, i) } loc(b, i) != null }
  // cerastes:axiom-ok 0035
  axiom member_inv { forall r: Ref, k: Int :: { member(r, k) } parent_of(member(r, k)) == r && index_of(member(r, k)) == k }
  // cerastes:axiom-ok 0036
  axiom member_lv { forall r: Ref, k: Int :: { lvloc(member(r, k)) } lvloc(member(r, k)) == lvloc(block_of(r)) }
}


// cerastes:trusted-contract allocation of int m[2][3] (S47 (x2)): the outer block of 2 slots, slot i's member 0 the inner block of 3; each permission one quantifier over two bound variables
method alloc_mat() returns (r: Ref)
  ensures ((r != null) && (r == loc(block_of(r), 0))) && (len(block_of(r)) == 2)
  ensures forall i: Int :: { loc(block_of(r), i) } (((0 <= i) && (i < 2))) ==> (len(member(loc(block_of(r), i), 0)) == 3)
  ensures forall i: Int, j: Int :: { loc(member(loc(block_of(r), i), 0), j) } (((0 <= i) && (i < 2)) && ((0 <= j) && (j < 3))) ==> acc(loc(member(loc(block_of(r), i), 0), j).v_int)
  ensures forall i: Int, j: Int :: { loc(member(loc(block_of(r), i), 0), j) } (((0 <= i) && (i < 2)) && ((0 <= j) && (j < 3))) ==> acc(loc(member(loc(block_of(r), i), 0), j).d_int)
  ensures forall i: Int, j: Int :: { loc(member(loc(block_of(r), i), 0), j) } (((0 <= i) && (i < 2)) && ((0 <= j) && (j < 3))) ==> (!loc(member(loc(block_of(r), i), 0), j).d_int)
  ensures (lvloc(block_of(r)) == loc(block_of(r), (-2))) && acc(lvloc(block_of(r)).lv)
  decreases _
method f_use()
{
  var vm: Ref
  var tin: Ref
  var tw: Ref
  var t4: Ref
  var t5: Int
  var t6: Perm
  var v_r: Int
  vm := alloc_mat()
  assert !((offset_of(vm) + 0 < 0) || (len(block_of(vm)) <= offset_of(vm) + 0)) //BOUND1
  tin := loc(member(loc(block_of(vm), offset_of(vm) + 0), 0), 0)
  assert !((offset_of(tin) + 3 < 0) || (len(block_of(tin)) <= offset_of(tin) + 3)) //BOUND2
  tw := loc(block_of(tin), offset_of(tin) + 3)
  assert perm(tw.v_int) > none //PERM
  assert tw.d_int //INIT
  v_r := tw.v_int
  assert forall i: Int, j: Int :: { loc(member(loc(block_of(vm), i), 0), j) } (((0 <= i) && (i < 2)) && ((0 <= j) && (j < 3))) ==> acc(loc(member(loc(block_of(vm), i), 0), j).v_int) //MARKED
  assert forall i: Int, j: Int :: { loc(member(loc(block_of(vm), i), 0), j) } (((0 <= i) && (i < 2)) && ((0 <= j) && (j < 3))) ==> acc(loc(member(loc(block_of(vm), i), 0), j).d_int) //MARKED
  assert perm(lvloc(block_of(vm)).lv) == write //LIVE
  exhale forall i: Int, j: Int :: { loc(member(loc(block_of(vm), i), 0), j) } (((0 <= i) && (i < 2)) && ((0 <= j) && (j < 3))) ==> acc(loc(member(loc(block_of(vm), i), 0), j).v_int)
  exhale forall i: Int, j: Int :: { loc(member(loc(block_of(vm), i), 0), j) } (((0 <= i) && (i < 2)) && ((0 <= j) && (j < 3))) ==> acc(loc(member(loc(block_of(vm), i), 0), j).d_int)
  exhale acc(lvloc(block_of(vm)).lv)
}

